1
00:00:00,146 --> 00:00:03,380
Hello, and a very warm welcome to Shah Spectrum.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:05,440
If you're new here, welcome.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:10,339
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us once more.

4
00:00:10,964 --> 00:00:16,515
What happens to the price of almost everything when one narrow stretch of water

5
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:18,574
stays disrupted for eight months?

6
00:00:18,574 --> 00:00:22,850
Since the twenty-eighth of February, the Strait of Hormuz has been in trouble, and

7
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:25,820
oil is still above one hundred dollars a barrel.

8
00:00:26,404 --> 00:00:31,714
Hi, I'm Mittal Shah, and this is my A-I voice, telling you today's story.

9
00:00:32,596 --> 00:00:34,141
Let's start with the place.

10
00:00:34,141 --> 00:00:38,262
The Strait of Hormuz is a channel between Iran and Oman.

11
00:00:38,262 --> 00:00:41,013
It is the only sea exit from the Persian Gulf.

12
00:00:41,013 --> 00:00:45,944
Before the war, about twenty million barrels of oil passed through it every day.

13
00:00:45,944 --> 00:00:49,118
That is roughly one fifth of all the oil the world uses.

14
00:00:49,118 --> 00:00:54,645
On Tuesday, Brent, the global benchmark price for crude oil, was trading at about

15
00:00:54,645 --> 00:00:57,673
one hundred and thirteen dollars a barrel.

16
00:00:58,297 --> 00:00:59,678
So why is it still stuck?

17
00:00:59,678 --> 00:01:02,898
Because each side wants the other to move first.

18
00:01:02,898 --> 00:01:07,861
Iran's position, as reported by its own media, is that the strait stays restricted

19
00:01:07,861 --> 00:01:11,155
until the United States meets a list of conditions.

20
00:01:11,155 --> 00:01:15,546
The first is that America ends its naval blockade of Iranian ports.

21
00:01:15,546 --> 00:01:19,938
A blockade means warships stop a country's ships from entering or leaving its

22
00:01:19,938 --> 00:01:20,538
harbours.

23
00:01:20,421 --> 00:01:25,812
Iran also wants relief from sanctions on its oil sales, and at least twelve billion

24
00:01:25,812 --> 00:01:28,230
dollars of frozen assets released.

25
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:32,340
The American side has not published its full response.

26
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:38,028
But reports say Washington wants Iran to make nuclear concessions first, and

27
00:01:38,028 --> 00:01:41,325
President Trump has said the blockade continues until a final deal.

28
00:01:41,848 --> 00:01:45,838
On Tuesday, Iran's security chief met the supreme leader.

29
00:01:45,838 --> 00:01:50,924
Iranian state media said he stressed keeping Iran's conditions for ending the war.

30
00:01:50,924 --> 00:01:55,753
Iran has also been talking with Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan.

31
00:01:55,753 --> 00:01:58,324
So there is talk, but no agreement.

32
00:01:58,971 --> 00:02:02,300
Now, why can't the world just route around the problem?

33
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,650
Some oil can.

34
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:09,397
Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates have pipelines that carry crude to ports

35
00:02:09,397 --> 00:02:10,820
outside the strait.

36
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:15,372
But they can carry only a part of what used to pass through.

37
00:02:15,372 --> 00:02:17,732
Ships are moving again in larger numbers.

38
00:02:17,732 --> 00:02:22,541
Even so, a think tank says October was the worst month yet for attacks on commercial

39
00:02:22,541 --> 00:02:23,907
shipping around the strait.

40
00:02:23,907 --> 00:02:29,612
And on Tuesday, Yemen's Houthi group said it hit a Saudi refinery.

41
00:02:29,612 --> 00:02:31,032
That claim is unconfirmed.

42
00:02:31,557 --> 00:02:36,284
Countries have also been drawing down emergency oil stockpiles to fill the gap, and

43
00:02:36,284 --> 00:02:38,566
those stocks are finite.

44
00:02:38,566 --> 00:02:40,283
Here is why that reaches your wallet.

45
00:02:40,283 --> 00:02:45,459
When oil cannot arrive, buyers around the world bid against each other for what is

46
00:02:45,459 --> 00:02:46,661
available.

47
00:02:46,661 --> 00:02:47,864
Prices rise.

48
00:02:47,864 --> 00:02:51,438
And refined fuels such as diesel can rise even faster than crude.

49
00:02:51,438 --> 00:02:56,613
Diesel runs trucks, tractors and ships, so it works its way into the cost of food

50
00:02:56,613 --> 00:02:57,213
and goods.

51
00:02:57,618 --> 00:02:58,713
Does this reach India?

52
00:02:58,713 --> 00:03:00,978
Yes, and there is a number for it.

53
00:03:00,978 --> 00:03:06,339
A research group, the Centre for Research on Energy and Clean Air, has estimated

54
00:03:06,339 --> 00:03:11,321
that India paid an extra twenty-two point five billion dollars for fossil fuel

55
00:03:11,321 --> 00:03:13,219
imports between March and August.

56
00:03:13,219 --> 00:03:15,022
Only China paid more.

57
00:03:15,022 --> 00:03:19,697
That is the group's estimate, and it leaves out shipping and insurance costs.

58
00:03:19,697 --> 00:03:25,377
One likely effect, and this is inference, is more pressure on what India pays for

59
00:03:25,377 --> 00:03:28,985
fuel, and on the rupee, for as long as prices stay high.

60
00:03:29,579 --> 00:03:31,698
There are limits to what we know.

61
00:03:31,698 --> 00:03:35,146
Iran's list of conditions comes from Iranian reporting.

62
00:03:35,146 --> 00:03:37,637
Washington's side is mostly unpublished.

63
00:03:37,637 --> 00:03:39,866
Oil prices change by the day.

64
00:03:39,866 --> 00:03:43,810
And nobody can say when a deal will come, or whether it will.

65
00:03:44,478 --> 00:03:45,429
To sum up:

66
00:03:45,429 --> 00:03:51,075
the strait is open in part, not in full, and oil stays expensive until the United

67
00:03:51,075 --> 00:03:53,706
States and Iran agree who moves first.

68
00:03:53,706 --> 00:03:58,811
So, that's the story, and thank you for spending these few minutes with me.

69
00:03:58,811 --> 00:04:01,692
Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

